module laed-criminal-local-rules.local-rules

import core.frcrimp45.{ frcrimp45 }
import frcrimp.deadlines.{ SentencingScheduled }

// The Eastern District of Louisiana's own criminal periods, counted under
// the criminal rules (FRCrimP 45(a) governs "any local rule"). No trigger
// carries a service method: FRCrimP 45(c)'s three added days follow the
// manner of service, which is not modeled here. A "working day" is
// counted as a court day.
//
// Periods that are FRCrimP periods stay in lit/frcrimp and are only named
// here: the presentence report's disclosure not less than 35 days before
// sentencing (LCrR 32.1(B); FRCrimP 32(e)(2)), the parties' written
// objections within 14 days thereafter (LCrR 32.1(B); FRCrimP 32(f)(1)),
// and the report with its addendum to the sentencing judge not later than
// seven days before the sentencing hearing (LCrR 32.1(D); FRCrimP 32(g)).
// The court may modify any LCrR 32.1 period for good cause, but the 14-day
// objection period may be diminished only with the defendant's consent
// (LCrR 32.1(F)). A presentence report is deemed disclosed when
// physically delivered, one day after its availability for inspection is
// orally communicated, or three days after a copy or notice of
// availability is mailed (LCrR 32.1(H)); the corpus models no such
// deemed-disclosure trigger, so it stays in this note.
//
// Conditions that are not deadlines from a modeled event stay in notes:
// discovery motions are filed within the time the magistrate judge sets
// and are noticed for hearing on the motion day following the expiration
// of 15 days, with a certificate that counsel conferred (LCrR 12); a
// continuance for an absent material witness needs an affidavit of the
// efforts made and the facts expected to be proved (LCrR 17); jurors may
// be interviewed only with leave of court (LCrR 23.2); a property bond
// needs equity not less than the principal amount of the bail set (LCrR
// 46.1(A)). The allotment of criminal matters to magistrate judges (LCrR
// 5.1, 5.2), the grand jury premises (LCrR 6.1, 6.2), building security
// (LCrR 43), law-student appearances (LCrR 44), extrajudicial statements
// (LCrR 53.1 to 53.10) and petty offenses (LCrR 58.1 to 58.3) state no
// period.
//
// The earlier E.D. La. criminal outline's FRCrimP flow and its decisions
// (United States v. Salerno, Brady v. Maryland, Barker v. Wingo, Zedner v.
// United States, Boykin v. Alabama, Missouri v. Frye, Jackson v. Virginia,
// United States v. Booker, Roe v. Flores-Ortega, Garza v. Idaho) are
// FRCrimP, Speedy Trial Act or constitutional authority and belong to
// lit/frcrimp; they are removed here: no reporter text is vendored.
/// The hearing date on which a pretrial discovery motion is noticed (E.D.
/// La. LCrR 12).
event DiscoveryMotionHearing()

/// E.D. La. LCrR 12: the government files its response to a pretrial
/// discovery motion no later than eight calendar days before the
/// scheduled hearing date.
deadline discovery-response: 8.days before DiscoveryMotionHearing() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. La. LCrR 12"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. La. LCrR 32.1.1: a motion or letter requesting a departure from
/// the Sentencing Guidelines is delivered to the sentencing judge's
/// chambers no later than 4:30 p.m. on the third working day before the
/// sentencing hearing; a request not timely submitted is deemed waived
/// unless good cause is shown. The 4:30 p.m. hour is not modeled.
deadline departure-request: 3.court_days before SentencingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. La. LCrR 32.1.1"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. La. LCrR 32.1.2: every other submission connected with sentencing
/// is filed no later than five working days before sentencing.
deadline sentencing-submission: 5.court_days before SentencingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. La. LCrR 32.1.2"
{
  forum frcrimp
}

/// E.D. La. LCrR 32.1.2: every response to a sentencing submission is
/// filed no later than three working days before sentencing.
deadline sentencing-response: 3.court_days before SentencingScheduled() counted_by frcrimp45 cite "E.D. La. LCrR 32.1.2"
{
  forum frcrimp
}
